<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vikings</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Viking</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Vikings were seafaring Scandinavians who raided, traded and settled across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> from the late eighth to the eleventh centuries. Their raids devastated the coasts and river valleys of the divided Carolingian kingdoms, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a> profile notes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-fat">Charles the Fat</a>'s payment of tribute to the Vikings besieging <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar Khaganate</a> profile notes that Khazar trade helped spread <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dirham">dirhams</a> into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-europe">Northern Europe</a>, a cornerstone of Viking commerce.</p></div>
